1
00:00:05,527 --> 00:00:07,730
Whiskers and the Moon Fish.

2
00:00:21,055 --> 00:00:26,448
Every morning, Whiskers the orange tabby did exactly one thing. Nothing at all.

3
00:00:31,829 --> 00:00:35,103
Whiskers! Wake up! The sun is already halfway up the sky!

4
00:00:35,303 --> 00:00:38,952
Five more minutes, Luna. Maybe five more hours.

5
00:00:43,297 --> 00:00:45,274
Was that... my breakfast bowl?

6
00:00:45,474 --> 00:00:48,640
It was. And now that you're awake, I have news. Big news.

7
00:00:51,603 --> 00:00:56,139
Old Tom from next door says there's a pond past the garden, beyond the meadow.

8
00:00:56,339 --> 00:01:00,435
And at night, a fish swims in it. A fish that glows like the moon itself.

9
00:01:00,635 --> 00:01:05,491
The Moon Fish. A fish so bright, they say, it lights up the whole pond.

10
00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:13,122
A glowing fish? Is it... tasty?

11
00:01:13,322 --> 00:01:16,032
Whiskers! It's a legend! Let's go and find it!

12
00:01:16,232 --> 00:01:18,419
Find it? That sounds like walking.

13
00:01:18,619 --> 00:01:20,166
There might be a snack at the end.

14
00:01:23,129 --> 00:01:24,530
Fine. Let's go.

15
00:01:28,184 --> 00:01:31,368
And so the two cats set off through the garden.

16
00:01:38,476 --> 00:01:40,359
Look, Whiskers! A butterfly!

17
00:01:49,194 --> 00:01:51,829
Come back here, you flappy little sandwich!

18
00:01:58,938 --> 00:02:01,468
You'll never catch it. It's much too fast for you.

19
00:02:01,668 --> 00:02:03,618
I let it win. On purpose.

20
00:02:07,273 --> 00:02:10,929
At the end of the garden stood the tall wooden fence.

21
00:02:11,129 --> 00:02:12,487
Up and over! Ready?

22
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:22,015
Cats were made for sleeping, not for climbing.

23
00:02:31,195 --> 00:02:33,357
Ta-da! Completely on purpose.

24
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:40,040
Beyond the fence lay a meadow of tall, whispering grass.

25
00:02:47,148 --> 00:02:48,555
Halt! Who goes there?

26
00:02:52,899 --> 00:02:54,854
Down here, Whiskers. It's a mouse!

27
00:02:55,054 --> 00:02:58,382
Not just a mouse. I am Pip, the bravest mouse in the meadow!

28
00:02:58,582 --> 00:03:01,918
Hello, Pip. Don't worry. We only eat fish today.

29
00:03:02,118 --> 00:03:04,154
Fish? You don't mean... the Moon Fish?

30
00:03:04,354 --> 00:03:05,474
You know about it?

31
00:03:05,674 --> 00:03:09,899
Everybody knows! But nobody has ever caught it. I'll show you the way to the pond!

32
00:03:17,007 --> 00:03:21,209
And so, the three new friends walked on as the sun went down.

33
00:03:36,952 --> 00:03:38,467
There it is. The pond.

34
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:40,770
Look! In the water! Something is glowing!

35
00:03:40,970 --> 00:03:43,806
The Moon Fish! It's real! And it's mine!

36
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:53,466
Whiskers wiggled. Whiskers waited. And then, Whiskers pounced!

37
00:04:02,301 --> 00:04:05,905
Blub! Where did it go? I had it! I definitely had it!

38
00:04:12,323 --> 00:04:13,752
Whiskers... look up.

39
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,319
It's not a fish at all. It's the moon!

40
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:26,737
The Moon Fish was only the reflection of the moon, shining in the water.

41
00:04:30,391 --> 00:04:33,044
So I just tried to catch... the sky?

42
00:04:42,916 --> 00:04:45,761
And everyone laughed. Even the frogs.

43
00:04:45,961 --> 00:04:49,342
We didn't find a Moon Fish, Whiskers. But we found a new friend.

44
00:04:49,542 --> 00:04:50,823
And I found two!

45
00:04:51,023 --> 00:04:54,566
Best adventure ever. Now can we go home and sleep?

46
00:04:58,911 --> 00:05:02,477
So the three friends walked home under the silver moon.

47
00:05:19,948 --> 00:05:25,133
That night, they curled up together on the windowsill, warm and dry and happy.

48
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:28,108
Goodnight, moon. Sorry I jumped on you.

49
00:05:35,217 --> 00:05:39,256
Because the best thing you find, is who you find along the way.

